":"B","text":"<div> <em>A</em> + 2<em>B</em> + 5<em>C</em> = 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>A </em>+ <em>B</em> + 5<em>C</em> = 1</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <em>A</em> + 2<em>B</em> + 5<em>C</em> = 0</div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/5f85807d2aa1bd836c343a28f791868c5bf1283b.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MCQ","correct":"B","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>The autocorrelation function of a wide sense stationary random process <img src=\"/media/d85e90a0f2d4153890e5a9c71c9baf96446fdb8d.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /> The value of <em>E</em>[<em>X</em>(5) – <em>X</em>(8)]<sup>2</sup> is</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> 50<em>e</em><sup>–15</sup></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> 50[1 – <em>e</em><sup>–15</sup>]</div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> 50[1 – <em>e</em><sup>–5</sup>]</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> 25<em>e</em><sup>–5</sup></div>","isCorrect":false}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(b)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/4dc788fd097b23468ae0cb94838859696364a66e.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Consider AM and PM singals having modulation indices ‘μ’ and ‘β’ respectively. The relation between ‘μ’ and ‘β’ to have the same noise performance for AM and PM receivers is,</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> β<sup>2</sup> + μ<sup>2</sup> = 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> β<sup>2</sup> – μ<sup>2</sup> = 1</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/f9e43708d9dc057841b41a0666b053f878040ba5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/8c31661c869b179d9c8c12296c99d88912f4c2e3.p